\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Meaning-based identity under $SE(2)$ frames. \textbf  {(a)} Every strict-$W^{\star }$ lock the semantic stack makes points at real water ($8/8$); the coordinate stack makes $992$ locks, all phantoms ($0/992$); frame recovery itself is exact in $80/80$ witness--traveler combinations. \textbf  {(b)} The failure asymmetry in worlds where identification is impossible (featureless band; a $180^\circ $-symmetric layout where the frame is unrecoverable in principle): semantic identity refuses to lock --- fails closed --- while coordinate identity keeps confidently locking wrong cells --- fails open.}}{6}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:identity}{{3}{6}{Meaning-based identity under $SE(2)$ frames. \textbf {(a)} Every strict-$\wstar $ lock the semantic stack makes points at real water ($8/8$); the coordinate stack makes $992$ locks, all phantoms ($0/992$); frame recovery itself is exact in $80/80$ witness--traveler combinations. \textbf {(b)} The failure asymmetry in worlds where identification is impossible (featureless band; a $180^\circ $-symmetric layout where the frame is unrecoverable in principle): semantic identity refuses to lock --- fails closed --- while coordinate identity keeps confidently locking wrong cells --- fails open}{figure.3}{}}
